Report an httpd A: or D: line whose address cannot be parsed.
Such a line is turned into a rule that denies every client, which is
the safe choice, but the message that would have said so is commented
out. A typo such as "A:192.168.1.300" made the server answer 403 to
everyone with nothing in the log to explain why.

Report it as a config error, as other bad lines are.

---
 networking/httpd.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/networking/httpd.c
+++ b/networking/httpd.c
@@ -951,7 +951,7 @@
 			if (scan_ip_mask(after_colon, &pip->ip, &pip->mask)) {
 				/* IP{/mask} syntax error detected, protect all */
 				ch = 'D';
-				//bb_error_msg("ERR");
+				bb_error_msg("config error '%s' in '%s'", buf, filename);
 				pip->ip = 0; /* could be set before error is detected - zero it (again) */
 				pip->mask = 0;
 			}
